{"reference":"Isaiah 32","book":"Isaiah","chapter":32,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Isaiah’s Textual Witnesses","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A nearly complete ancient manuscript of Isaiah, the Great Isaiah Scroll, broadly agrees with the Masoretic form of the book while differing from it in many spellings and some substantive readings. Other Isaiah manuscripts and interpretive writings from Qumran also show that the book was copied and interpreted actively. The precise significance of these differences remains disputed.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_032_1a43b9ccb06bb8c10383b061"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}